# Production build configuration (loaded automatically by `vite build`).
#
# Proxy mode: VITE_API_BASE is empty, so the browser calls a RELATIVE URL
# (/api/v1/chat/pipeline). A reverse proxy in front of the static bundle
# (see deploy/nginx.conf) forwards /api to the Spring Boot backend.
#
# Why this over direct mode for production:
#   - the backend URL is NOT baked into the shipped JS (no internal-topology leak)
#   - no CORS configuration needed on the backend
#   - TLS is terminated at the edge; the browser only ever speaks HTTPS
#
# To build in direct mode instead, set the absolute HTTPS URL of the backend:
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://api.venera.uz
VITE_API_BASE=
